  "term": "seasonal affective disorder",
  "definition": "Seasonal affective disorder is a pattern of depression that returns at the same time each year, most often in winter. It may also involve anxiety, irritability, low energy, sleeping longer, increased appetite especially for carbohydrates, and weight gain.",
